          }
        },
        "80d3ee7d-e860-4a9c-8b84-2c5508cdf136": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Maintenance",
            "text": "<p><strong>General Maintenance</strong><br/><br/>1. When work has finished, remove plant residues adhering to the wheels, inside the ventilation opening, the grass ejector opening and the cylinder. Do not use hard or pointed objects for this purpose as they could damage the machine.<br/><br/>2. To ensure that the safety guard flap closes properly, remove any earth that may have collected<br/>on the safety guard springs and/or the housing.<br/><br/>3. Completely empty the collection bag.<br/><br/>4. Always keep the machine clean. Do not use cleaning agents or solvents. We cannot be held liable for damage caused by our machines if they were improperly repaired, if non-original parts have been used or if they were used not in keeping with their intended purpose.<br/><br/><strong>Storing the Machine</strong><br/><br/>The device features the following storage options to save space:<br/><br/>1. Before storing your machine, disconnect the plug from the power socket. Remove the collection bag.<br/><br/>2. Loosen the wing knobs on both sides of the handle bars.<br/><br/>3. Fold the upper and centre handles. Making sure that the cables do not become trapped.<br/><br/>4. Store the machine indoors in a cool, dry location and out of reach of children.<br/><br/>5. Allow the motor to cool before storing the equipment in a confined space.<br/><br/>6. Do not cover the equipment as moisture could build up.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
